        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: accidō, accidere",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "accidō, accidere — \"to happen\". Quid accidit? — \"What happened?\" Its perfect is spelled like its present in this form: accidit. It is ad + cadō, \"to fall towards\", the source of English accident."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "accidō is ad, \"towards\", with cadō, \"to fall\" (Lewis & Short), its a weakened to i: to fall towards, to befall. It is a different word from accīdō, \"to cut into\", built on caedō, \"to cut\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
